  "worked_solution": "Let's recall our definitions.\n\n- The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers: $1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…$\n\n- The integers consist of all of the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of all numbers that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $-\\frac{1}{9}$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $-\\frac{1}{9}$ is not an integer.\n\n- $-\\frac{1}{9}$ is a rational number because it can be written as $\\frac{(-1)}{9}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
